{"name":"Woven Navajo","hex":"#cead8e","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"woven","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Fabricated by weaving.","Interlaced"]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A cloth formed by weaving. It only stretches in the bias directions (between the warp and weft directions), unless the threads are elastic."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/woven"}],"entries":[{"title":"Woven fabric","blocks":[{"text":"Woven fabric is any textile formed by weaving. Woven fabrics, often created on a loom, are made of many threads woven in a warp and weft. Technically, a woven fabric is any fabric made by interlacing two or more threads at right angles to one another."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Palaung_Woman_Kalaw_Shan_Myanmar.jpg/330px-Palaung_Woman_Kalaw_Shan_Myanmar.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Woven_fabric"},{"title":"Navajo","blocks":[{"text":"The Navajo are an Indigenous People of the Southwestern United States. The Navajo term for themselves is Diné. Their language is Navajo, a Southern Athabaskan language. The states with the largest Diné populations are Arizona (140,263) and New Mexico (108,305). More than three-quarters of the Diné population resides in these two states."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/ff/Manuelito.jpg/330px-Manuelito.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Navajo"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/Fabric_yarn_fiber.PNG/500px-Fabric_yarn_fiber.PNG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/67/Fabric_yarn_fiber.PNG/500px-Fabric_yarn_fiber.PNG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"An Arabic-l